6a. Strongly criticises the Commission for its delay in handling the infringement procedure against Italy on the serious violations of EU law, notably the breach of the Industrial Emissions Directive1a, arising from the management of the ILVA steel plant, which is the biggest steel plant in Europe; regrets that, although the Commission launched the infringement procedure concerned (INFR(2013)2177) in 2013 and although the area surrounding the ILVA steel plant persistently recorded high levels of cardiovascular, respiratory and carcinogenic diseases, including in children, with fatal effects in many cases, as well as very high levels of air pollutants, in more than a decade the Commission never brought this case before the CJEU, a delay that has been repeatedly denounced by petitioners;

---

1a Directive 2010/75/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council of 24 November 2010 on industrial emissions (OJ L 334, 17.12.2010, p. 17, ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2010/75/oj).
